  "platform_findings": {
    "ubuntu": "The native vault-selection screen opened, but preparing private per-vault app data failed with ENOENT and the app returned to No vault is open. The same failure reproduced in the Ubuntu-only rerun; this SHA did not yet log which preparation operation failed.",
    "windows": "Open vault remained IsEnabled=false throughout the 10-second UI Automation poll. A physical screen click did not produce a new picker window, although the foreground screenshot showed the button. The timeout threw before the new control-inventory diagnostic could be included in the report.",
    "macos": "The native panel appeared and Escape returned to the active vault. The strict app-data snapshot differed because eframe's app.ron file appeared after startup. The report captured its raw contents; it stores window position/size and egui state. The observed timing is consistent with normal eframe persistence, but does not by itself establish cancellation as the cause.",
    "quality": "The shared tesseract invocation helper resolved the prior Knip failure; quality passed on all three operating systems."
  },
  "correction": "Add path-free operation-stage context to per-vault app-data preparation errors; let Windows picker polling time out into the diagnostic report; establish the macOS startup-persistence baseline before cancellation and continue requiring an unchanged snapshot after cancellation and close.",
